{
  "requirement": "Every requirement defined by a fenced `{req}` directive in a chapter under the configured mdBook source directory MUST have an evidence file named `evidence/<full-requirement-name>.json`. The full name MUST use the chapter's path-derived namespace followed by the directive name; for example, a directive named `check` in `md/requirements.md` has the full name `requirements.check`. Habeas MUST apply this rule to its own requirements in this chapter.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The coverage check itself is correct and tested. The one gap is incomplete `{impl}` marking of the code that derives the chapter namespace.\n\n**What works**\n- `inspect_repository_with_progress` (src/evidence.rs:170-295, `{impl}` at line 243):\n  - It reads the source directory from `book.toml` through `book_source_dir`.\n  - It collects definitions with `collect_definitions`.\n  - It reports `evidence/<name>.json: missing for requirement …` for every non-term definition (requirements and examples) that has no evidence file directly under `evidence/`.\n  - Only a file at `evidence/<name>.json` counts as present.\n- `files_with_extension` (src/evidence.rs:497-549) walks the book source directory for chapters and is marked `{impl}`.\n- `full_requirement_name` (src/lib.rs:498-506) joins the namespace and directive name and is marked `{impl}`.\n- Habeas applies the rule to its own requirements. `tests/habeas.rs` runs `habeas::validate()` on the repository itself.\n- Tests cover the main cases:\n  - `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` (src/evidence.rs:1474) uses a nested chapter, `md/reqs/foo/bar.md`, and accepts `evidence/foo.bar.ready.json` as the full name `foo.bar.ready`.\n  - `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` (src/evidence.rs:1507) asserts the `missing for requirement` error for requirements with no evidence file.\n  - Other tests cover `book.src` handling.\n\n**Gap: incomplete `{impl}` marking**\n- The requirement says the full name \"MUST use the chapter's path-derived namespace\". That derivation is done by `chapter_namespace` in src/lib.rs (about lines 257-276). It strips the extension and joins the path components with dots.\n- That function carries only `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.identifiers`. It has no `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.coverage`.\n- `ci.identifiers` specifies only the `reqs/` prefix and `index`/`README` omissions. The base path-to-namespace mapping, which gives `md/requirements.md` → `requirements.check`, is stated only by `coverage`.\n- This is inconsistent. The trivial join in `full_requirement_name` is marked for `coverage`, but the function that actually derives the namespace is not.\n- `collect_definitions`, which finds the directives in chapters under the source directory, is also not marked for `coverage`. The `SUMMARY.md` skip it contains is likewise not tied to this requirement.\n- Under the criterion that code implementing part of a requirement without an `{impl}` reference is a gap, this is a gap. No `FIXME` acknowledges it.",
  "inputs": [
